forwarding-race.log (also includes XLSX tests):
CGO_ENABLED=1 GOEXPERIMENT=greenteagc,jsonv2 GOMAXPROCS=4 go test -p 2 -race -tags unit ./internal/service -run 'Test(AnthropicBuffered|WSComparable|AnthropicSSEDelta|AppendRawJSON|ShouldKeepIngress|NormalizeOpenAIWSPayload|HandleResponsesBufferedStreamingResponse|HandleCCBufferedFromAnthropic|Claude55ResponsesSignedThinking|AnthropicNative|GatewayService_Streaming|HandleStreamingResponse|UsageExport)' -count=1

Benchmarks compare the previous algorithms retained in test-only helpers against
the new production implementations, using identical inputs in the same binary.
legacy=true is the previous implementation, legacy=false is the new implementation.
Three rounds per case. Tool/text benchmark fragments are 256 bytes.
XLSX benchmark writes 1,000 rows to io.Discard per operation, including ZIP close.

The WSL-based initial test command could not start because WSL was unavailable;
it was cancelled before execution. The same Go version/experiments were used on
Windows. No production upstream/model, database, or Engine was used in these tests.
